.TH "YAMLR-SECURE" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBSynthesize Least-Privilege Network Policies\fR
.PP
The \fByamlr secure\fR command analyzes Service definitions, workload selectors, and active ingress topologies to automatically synthesize least-privilege Kubernetes \fBNetworkPolicy\fR manifests, establishing zero-trust network boundaries across namespaces.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
# Analyze services in current directory and generate network policies
yamlr secure .

# Generate policies for specific directory and save to file
yamlr secure ./k8s -o ./k8s/network-policies.yaml
.RE
.fi
.SH "OPTIONS & FLAGS"
.SS "Positional Arguments"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB[PATH]\fR: Manifest directory or file containing Kubernetes Services and workloads (defaults to \fB.\fR).
.SS "Output Controls"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB-o, --output <PATH>\fR: File path where generated \fBNetworkPolicy\fR manifests should be written. If omitted, generated policies are printed to stdout.
.SH "SECURITY ARCHITECTURE"
1. \fBService Topology Discovery\fR: Discovers all \fBService\fR resources, their target ports, protocols (TCP/UDP), and selector labels.
.PP
2. \fBNamespace Isolation\fR: Scopes policies to workload namespaces to restrict lateral cluster movement.
.PP
3. \fBLeast-Privilege Ingress\fR: Generates ingress rules permitting only explicit traffic matching defined Service endpoints.
.PP
.SH "EXIT CODES"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB0\fR (\fBEXIT_SUCCESS\fR): Policies synthesized successfully.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB1\fR (\fBEXIT_VIOLATIONS\fR): Specified target path does not exist.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fB124\fR (\fBEXIT_SYSTEM_ERROR\fR): Manifest discovery or file read failure.
